igin/tickets ref update during snapshot fetch; a normal retry completed successfully without force.","timestamp":1787445397242472001}],"created_at":1787417237300883001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6c5f4d13-9f01-4e98-8619-1230a2afe09f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e0d5-6821-6aa3-4fe6"}],"description":"## Context\nThe MCP reference generator selects the first physical description line. Wrapped registrar prose therefore yields truncated summaries. The accepted first-line choice is recorded on `lupine-clearcut-mare`. The `transition_ticket` registrar also says close classes are ignored for non-bug tickets although the administrative subset is supported.\n\n## Plan\n- Normalize the complete first description paragraph into one generated summary.\n- Stop summary extraction at the next paragraph.\n- Correct the `transition_ticket` registrar description without changing its schema or behavior.\n- Regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md`.\n- Add focused generator and registrar contract tests.\n- Do not add duplicate summary metadata or a general prose validator.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every generated MCP summary is a complete first paragraph rather than a physical-line fragment.\n- [x] Wrapped descriptions render as one complete summary.\n- [x] Paragraphs after the summary remain excluded.\n- [x] `transition_ticket` documents bug classifications and the non-bug administrative subset accurately.\n- [x] Generated-reference and focused MCP tests pass.\n- [x] MCP schemas and runtime behavior are unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"Generate summaries from complete first paragraphs."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"Correct transition tool description."},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate MCP summaries."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"Pin wrapped and multi-paragraph summary behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"